32: {"hash":"c3b18bb7300e2361a554934dc2b399e0ea58894226286a972fe5c39228e54e40","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-2006.10726","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-2006.10726","published_date":"2020-06-18","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.10726v1","text":"The v1 study adapts a pretrained predictive model using unlabeled target inputs, without source examples. Its objective reduces predictive entropy and its adjustable components are feature-wise affine modulations. Experiments concern image/digit classification. The method discussion explicitly also allows compatible probabilistic regressors with predictive variance; therefore 'entropy adaptation is categorically impossible for regression' misstates this source. That observation does not automatically provide a distribution or useful entropy objective for a deterministic scalar regressor. Claims of benefit remain scoped to the source's evaluated settings.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"Fully Test-time Adaptation by Entropy Minimization","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"f86fc5e4010647a5ad2f645f6141dfd64f85b28d3536bbc0086a65f9dfb51824"},"previous_hash":"ca356dffcc6a99fa674215abc79dda1336e3f92fbfca60e94c4374802eca6e90","sequence":31,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.518969+00:00"}
33: {"hash":"99a8fb5e19729908251d57d4c6aa62c7d20024a7dcf351153e4b22681a9ad640","kind":"tool_requested","payload":{"arguments":{"document_id":"doc-2002.08546"},"name":"literature.read"},"previous_hash":"c3b18bb7300e2361a554934dc2b399e0ea58894226286a972fe5c39228e54e40","sequence":32,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.526013+00:00"}
34: {"hash":"880db09da458c97d039909c52c65f557655c9f4f7f65c35aa82ff4bc1588678c","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-2002.08546","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-2002.08546","published_date":"2020-02-20","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2002.08546v1","text":"SHOT studies source-free unsupervised domain adaptation for classification: retain the trained classifier while adapting a target feature extractor without source examples. Information maximization combines confident individual predictions with diversity across the target collection; self-supervised pseudo-label refinement is another component. Its setting is not identical to one-pass adaptation of a scalar regressor. Class probabilities, class diversity and pseudo-label definitions must be distinguished from continuous regression outputs. The source is evidence that source-free adaptation is already studied, not proof that all source-free tasks are solved.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"Do We Really Need to Access the Source Data? Source Hypothesis Transfer for Unsupervised Domain Adaptation","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"9caa29bb99a39ec92cd75f0651201c789ea52a6961e152c54602f56beb373264"},"previous_hash":"99a8fb5e19729908251d57d4c6aa62c7d20024a7dcf351153e4b22681a9ad640","sequence":33,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.531065+00:00"}
35: {"hash":"a7ad2da1444bcee7420f4c860c8c9832c022de3891cbfe3042ab2adafc5217c2","kind":"tool_requested","payload":{"arguments":{"document_id":"doc-1909.13231"},"name":"literature.read"},"previous_hash":"880db09da458c97d039909c52c65f557655c9f4f7f65c35aa82ff4bc1588678c","sequence":34,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.536971+00:00"}
36: {"hash":"e66be2d93c4667b33105f11ad9839a6752456f55912db66fbe6d7b07ab98d812","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-1909.13231","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-1909.13231","published_date":"2019-09-29","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.13231v1","text":"Test-time training jointly prepares a main prediction task and an auxiliary self-supervised task sharing a feature extractor. At deployment the auxiliary loss updates shared parameters using unlabeled input. Rotation prediction is the image-specific example, not a universal requirement. Standard per-instance and stateful online variants differ in whether updates are retained. The paper gives a convex-model discussion involving gradient alignment; this is not an unconditional guarantee of improvement for any auxiliary task. The preparation stage and availability of a suitable self-supervised task differ from adapting an arbitrary off-the-shelf checkpoint.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"Test-Time Training for Out-of-Distribution Generalization","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"5e1b806993b4943befadae6efe9c070a117977273bad5eb266716537acb02f22"},"previous_hash":"a7ad2da1444bcee7420f4c860c8c9832c022de3891cbfe3042ab2adafc5217c2","sequence":35,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.545064+00:00"}
37: {"hash":"09edd57f7ffb5e450e6697ecace7df98502dd79fd71f70a3b6305c060be81ca7","kind":"tool_requested","payload":{"arguments":{"document_id":"doc-1607.01719"},"name":"literature.read"},"previous_hash":"e66be2d93c4667b33105f11ad9839a6752456f55912db66fbe6d7b07ab98d812","sequence":36,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.550474+00:00"}
38: {"hash":"db46e5f675bd0ba09c2970c036c1796ce216db1dd5bdba608ae5d07295e9202e","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-1607.01719","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-1607.01719","published_date":"2016-07-06","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1607.01719v1","text":"Deep CORAL penalizes differences between source and target feature covariance matrices while learning deep representations. Its training setup combines labeled source data and unlabeled target data, unlike deployment with only a source model. The covariance-matching objective gives prior art for feature-distribution alignment but does not by itself establish a source-free deployment procedure or guarantee preservation of a regression function. The paper also situates covariance matching among related distribution-alignment approaches; alignment is not a novel concept merely because used in a new proposal.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"Deep CORAL: Correlation Alignment for Deep Domain Adaptation","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"c6fcb8621ef7a5a0433c3383a81e40376c32da6970c7edb33966c11afdfc922f"},"previous_hash":"09edd57f7ffb5e450e6697ecace7df98502dd79fd71f70a3b6305c060be81ca7","sequence":37,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.559571+00:00"}
39: {"hash":"1a60a8ad7122ea2b876df6a084894a23d20e8eabc5353082cdaaafb70cea7e0c","kind":"tool_requested","payload":{"arguments":{"document_id":"doc-1505.07818"},"name":"literature.read"},"previous_hash":"db46e5f675bd0ba09c2970c036c1796ce216db1dd5bdba608ae5d07295e9202e","sequence":38,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.570566+00:00"}
40: {"hash":"488a56002b26f5e72d69e7130abcd97d1361f9028f88c0a607a1c4657aafc707","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-1505.07818","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-1505.07818","published_date":"2015-05-28","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1505.07818v1","text":"Domain-adversarial learning trains representations to support labeled-source prediction while reducing a domain classifier's ability to distinguish source and target examples. A gradient-reversal component implements the adversarial update. The study uses source examples and unlabeled target examples during training, so it is not directly a source-free test-time method. Domain indistinguishability and task-discriminative structure play different roles. This broader adaptation prior art is relevant for comparing information assumptions, not proof of feasibility under stricter deployment constraints.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"Domain-Adversarial Training of Neural Networks","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"2514ad2e067c3f01fe68405a443743f495fdcd39cb4fd0ad6f944484375f0f2a"},"previous_hash":"1a60a8ad7122ea2b876df6a084894a23d20e8eabc5353082cdaaafb70cea7e0c","sequence":39,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.582519+00:00"}
41: {"hash":"f16ee01bc75b17554ce97ea2ea891aee308cb552c89d9d36cfcf0b6be2638372","kind":"tool_requested","payload":{"arguments":{"document_id":"doc-1502.03167"},"name":"literature.read"},"previous_hash":"488a56002b26f5e72d69e7130abcd97d1361f9028f88c0a607a1c4657aafc707","sequence":40,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.589563+00:00"}
42: {"hash":"0f9953a48d5ab3abf94a729ef83cd7dd5b6a276416ccd462841f7ad373e19c99","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-1502.03167","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-1502.03167","published_date":"2015-02-11","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1502.03167v1","text":"Batch normalization normalizes activations using mini-batch statistics and learns a scale and offset per activation channel. Training and inference statistics must be distinguished. This is architectural and optimization background, not itself evidence of successful target-domain adaptation. The source attributes its training benefits to reducing internal covariate shift; a survey should distinguish that source's interpretation from an established universal explanation or a guarantee under external distribution shift.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"Batch Normalization: Accelerating Deep Network Training by Reducing Internal Covariate Shift","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"894fbe65ba658f4856db978f8c43b9665d00b4b7d84f55aa454f1a44e5265c3c"},"previous_hash":"f16ee01bc75b17554ce97ea2ea891aee308cb552c89d9d36cfcf0b6be2638372","sequence":41,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.595563+00:00"}
43: {"hash":"aeaeeefc385e7e661f1eecb70f9d131d815ea441a8ece099eb90ded7c6ea8edc","kind":"tool_requested","payload":{"arguments":{"document_id":"doc-1706.04599"},"name":"literature.read"},"previous_hash":"0f9953a48d5ab3abf94a729ef83cd7dd5b6a276416ccd462841f7ad373e19c99","sequence":42,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.603565+00:00"}
44: {"hash":"885b8d19fde1838a51d8c3ae17b62229d991a958e733bf4cd0a6338935dede48","kind":"tool_completed","payload":{"name":"literature.read","result":{"document_id":"doc-1706.04599","full_text_access":"literature.read_page(document_id, page_number); one-based PDF page","paper_id":"background-arxiv-1706.04599","published_date":"2017-06-14","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.04599v1","text":"This classification calibration study distinguishes prediction confidence from empirical correctness, reports miscalibration in modern networks, and evaluates post-processing methods such as temperature scaling. Calibration fitting uses a labeled validation set, unlike label-free target adaptation. It is useful background against equating confidence with correctness, but is not a direct experiment on adaptation of deterministic regression models. Neither calibration quality nor increased confidence alone establishes improved target regression error.","text_kind":"maintainer_written_digest_not_full_paper","title":"On Calibration of Modern Neural Networks","version":"arxiv-v1"},"result_hash":"581410eaf482989642b39e94019161a12d710f5bcdd5f910c0854d14f48c8a96"},"previous_hash":"aeaeeefc385e7e661f1eecb70f9d131d815ea441a8ece099eb90ded7c6ea8edc","sequence":43,"time_utc":"2026-09-23T05:49:01.614565+00:00"}
